{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "heat_2d_x_periodic_o4",
    "description": "MMS driver: 2-D heat equation reduced to x-diffusion u_t = alpha u_xx on the unit box [0,1]x[0,1] with a PERIODIC x-boundary, discretized by grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2x_4_periodic (fourth-order centered second derivative, periodic wrap) over the full 2-D field u[x,y]. Manufactured DECAYING solution u(x,y,t) = exp(-alpha (2 pi)^2 t) cos(2 pi x): zonally periodic (period 1 on the unit box) and constant in y. Derivation: cos(2 pi x) has u_xx = -(2 pi)^2 cos(2 pi x), so u_t = -alpha (2 pi)^2 u = alpha u_xx exactly for the continuous PDE; on the periodic x-circle cos(2 pi x_i) is an exact eigenvector of the discrete circulant fourth-order second-difference operator, so the discretization error is pure O(dx^4) truncation of the eigenvalue and the diffusion is dissipative (stable). The y axis is PASSIVE: u is constant in y, no y-operator appears, NY closed to 8 at the import edge; NX stays open (grid default 64, rebound by the convergence sweep via the loader API). Geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm) fulfilled for the unit box: x0=y0=0, dx=1/NX (an observed dividing by the metaparameter name NX, substituted as an integer literal at load per esm-spec 9.7.6 so the sweep keeps dx consistent), dy=1/NY. BUILD-TIME SCOPE CAVEAT (AGENTS.md): the free-name dx survives only in the runtime rule body; the ic and test references spell the cell-center coordinate x_i = 0 + (i-1/2)(1/NX) inline from literals and the metaparameter NX (the build-time cellwise evaluator is scope-free), never invoking the grid's x_coord free-name template.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:problem", "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d", "equation:heat", "mms"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Fornberg, B. (1988). Generation of finite difference formulas on arbitrarily spaced grids. Mathematics of Computation 51(184), 699-706.",
        "doi": "10.1090/S0025-5718-1988-0935077-0"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Heat2DxPeriodicO4": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D2x_4_periodic.esm",
          "bindings": { "NY": 8 }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": { "type": "state", "units": "K", "shape": ["x", "y"], "description": "Temperature field over the 2-D [x, y] index sets (constant in y in this problem)." },
        "alpha": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m^2/s", "default": 0.01, "description": "Thermal diffusivity." },
        "x0": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m", "default": 0, "description": "Left x domain edge a = 0 (unit box): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm)." },
        "y0": { "type": "parameter", "units": "m", "default": 0, "description": "Bottom y domain edge (unit box): the grid's y0 free name (unused here; the solution is constant in y)." },
        "dx": { "type": "observed", "units": "m", "expression": { "op": "/", "args": [1, "NX"] }, "description": "x-spacing 1/NX: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. NX is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent." },
        "dy": { "type": "observed", "units": "m", "expression": { "op": "/", "args": [1, "NY"] }, "description": "y-spacing 1/NY: the grid's dy free name; NY closed to 8 at the import edge (unused here; the x-second-derivative rule references only dx)." }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "ic", "args": ["u"] },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" }, "j": { "from": "y" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "cos",
              "args": [
                { "op": "*", "args": [6.283185307179586, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "NX"] }] }] }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "t" },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "alpha",
              { "op": "D", "args": [ { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "x" } ], "wrt": "x" }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_heat_x_periodic_o4_decay",
          "description": "Manufactured solution u(x,y,t) = exp(-alpha (2 pi)^2 t) cos(2 pi x) with alpha = 0.01. The cosine mode gives u_t = -alpha (2 pi)^2 u_cos and u_xx = -(2 pi)^2 u_cos (so u_t = alpha u_xx) with periodic x-wrap, constant in y. The discrete circulant fourth-order periodic operator has cos(2 pi x_i) as an exact eigenvector, so the error is pure O(dx^4) eigenvalue truncation; the operator is dissipative, so the decay stays clean at t=0.1. References evaluate at cell centers x_i = (i - 1/2)/NX, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the relative L2 error. Exact per-resolution errors pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/heat_2d_x_periodic_o4/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.1 },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 1e-9 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" }, "j": { "from": "y" } },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "cos",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "*", "args": [6.283185307179586, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "NX"] }] }] }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 1e-4 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": { "i": { "from": "x" }, "j": { "from": "y" } },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "exp", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": [-0.01, 39.47841760435743, 0.1] }] },
                    { "op": "cos", "args": [{ "op": "*", "args": [6.283185307179586, { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] }, { "op": "/", "args": [1, "NX"] }] }] }] }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
